  {
   "id": 676921,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "An advertisement that is visually appealing and emphasizes quality of life, people, and relationships is an example of which of Hofstede’s cultural dimensions?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1344936,
     "content_html": "Femininity",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "An advertisement that is visually appealing and emphasizes quality of life, people, and relationships is an example of femininity."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344935,
     "content_html": "Masculinity",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Gender can strongly impact the creative concept and messaging behind marketing promotions, ads, and social media. Achievement, power, and strength are considered masculine traits."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344934,
     "content_html": "Uncertainty avoidance",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. Uncertainty avoidance, or a high dislike for ambiguity and the unknown, is not just an individual trait; it is a characteristic of societies in general. It is not related to the Hofstede dimension related to quality of life."
    },
    {
     "id": 1344933,
     "content_html": "Short-term orientation",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "That&#8217;s not correct. The short-term dimension describes how individuals believe and behave in society. It is also based on links to the past and challenges in the future. Short-term cultures focus more on personal steadiness, happiness, and stability."
    }
   ],
